.TH "FONTFACE.SIZEADJUST" "3JS" "November 3, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
FontFace.sizeAdjust \- FontFace: sizeAdjust property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sizeAdjust\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]FontFace\f[R]
interface represents a multiplier for the font\(cqs glyph outlines and
metrics, such as glyph widths and line heights, used to lay out text.
.PP
Different fonts can look larger or smaller at the same font size,
because each font\(cqs glyphs are drawn at a different size relative to
that font size.
The \f[CR]sizeAdjust\f[R] property allows you to scale a font to match
the apparent size of another font, such as a fallback font that is shown
until a web font loads.
.PP
It is equivalent to the \f[CR]\(atfont\-face/size\-adjust\f[R]
descriptor of \f[CR]\(atfont\-face\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A string containing a non\-negative percentage, such as
\f[CR]\(dq120%\(dq\f[R].
The default value is \f[CR]\(dq100%\(dq\f[R], which leaves the font\(cqs
glyph outlines and metrics unchanged.
.PP
This property accepts the same values as the
\f[CR]\(atfont\-face/size\-adjust\f[R] descriptor.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown when setting the property to a value that doesn\(cqt match the
syntax of the \f[CR]\(atfont\-face/size\-adjust\f[R] descriptor, such as
a negative percentage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Setting the size adjustment
This example sets the size adjustment when constructing a font face,
then updates it using the property.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] fontFace = \f[B]new\f[R] FontFace(
  \(dqRoboto\(dq,
  \(aqurl(\(dqhttps://fonts.example.com/roboto.woff2\(dq)\(aq,
  {
    sizeAdjust: \(dq120%\(dq,
  },
);
console.log(fontFace.sizeAdjust); \f[I]// \(dq120%\(dq\f[R]

fontFace.sizeAdjust = \(dq100%\(dq;
console.log(fontFace.sizeAdjust); \f[I]// \(dq100%\(dq\f[R]
.EE
